1→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   452→                        TechCrunch reports that Mark Zuckerberg told Meta staff that AI agents haven't progressed as quickly as he'd hoped, suggesting a potential cooling of expectations around autonomous AI agent capabilities.\n   453→                    </div>\n   454→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   455→                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/07/02/mark-zuckerberg-tells-staff-that-ai-agents-havent-progressed-as-quickly-as-hed-hoped/\">Lucas Ropek</a>\n   456→                        | 2026-07-02\n   457→                    </div>\n   458→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   459→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI-agents</span>\n   460→                        <span class=\"tag\">Meta</span>\n   461→                        <span class=\"tag\">expectations</span>\n   462→                    </div>\n   463→                </div>\n   464→\n   465→                <div class=\"item\">\n   466→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   467→                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-07-01-kimi-k2-7-is-now-available-in-github-copilot/\">Kimi K2.7 Code Now Available in GitHub Copilot</a>\n   468→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">TechMedia</span>\n   469→                    </div>\n   470→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   471→                        GitHub announces that Kimi K2.7 Code model is now generally available in GitHub Copilot, representing continued evolution of AI coding assistant capabilities.\n   472→                    </div>\n   473→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   474→                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-07-01-kimi-k2-7-is-now-available-in-github-copilot/\">GitHub Blog</a>\n   475→                        | 2026-07-02\n   476→                    </div>\n   477→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   478→                        <span class=\"tag\">GitHub-Copilot</span>\n   479→                        <span class=\"tag\">Kimi-K2.7</span>\n   480→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI-coding</span>\n   481→                    </div>\n   482→                </div>\n   483→\n   484→                <div class=\"item\">\n   485→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   486→                        <a href=\"https://senior-swe-bench.snorkel.ai/\">Senior SWE-Bench: Benchmark for AI Agents</a>\n   487→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   488→                    </div>\n   489→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   490→                        New open-source benchmark 'Senior SWE-Bench' launched to assess AI agents at senior engineer level, showing maturation of evaluation methods for AI coding capabilities.\n   491→                    </div>\n   492→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   493→                        <a href=\"https://senior-swe-bench.snorkel.ai/\">Snorkel AI</a>\n   494→                        | 2026-07-02\n   495→                    </div>\n   496→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   497→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI-benchmarking</span>\n   498→                        <span class=\"tag\">senior-engineers</span>\n   499→                        <span class=\"tag\">evaluation</span>\n   500→                    </div>\n   501→                </div>\n   502→\n   503→                <div class=\"item\">\n   504→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   505→                        <a href=\"https://blog.okturtles.org/2026/07/short-leash-ai-method/\">The Short Leash AI Coding Method for Beating Fable</a>\n   506→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Blog</span>\n   507→                    </div>\n   508→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   509→                        New methodology document for constrained AI coding approaches, reflecting emerging best practices for controlling and directing AI coding assistants for optimal results.\n   510→                    </div>\n   511→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   512→                        <a href=\"https://blog.okturtles.org/2026/07/short-leash-ai-method/\">okturtles.org</a>\n   513→                        | 2026-07-02\n   514→                    </div>\n   515→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   516→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI-coding</span>\n   517→                        <span class=\"tag\">methodology</span>\n   518→                        <span class=\"tag\">best-practices</span>\n   519→                    </div>\n   520→                </div>\n   521→\n   522→                <div class=\"item\">\n   523→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   524→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/HUANGCHIHHUNGLeo/claude-real-video\">Claude Real Video: Any LLM Can Watch a Video</a>\n   525→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n   526→                    </div>\n   527→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   528→                        New open-source project 'Claude-real-video' enables any LLM to process video content, expanding multimodal capabilities and accessibility of video understanding for AI models.\n   529→                    </div>\n   530→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   531→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/HUANGCHIHHUNGLeo/claude-real-video\">HUANGCHIHHUNGLeo</a>\n   532→                        | 2026-07-02\n   533→                    </div>\n   534→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   535→                        <span class=\"tag\">video-processing</span>\n   536→                        <span class=\"tag\">multimodal-AI</span>\n   537→                        <span class=\"tag\">open-source</span>\n   538→                    </div>\n   539→                </div>\n   540→\n   541→                <div class=\"item\">\n   542→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   543→                        <a href=\"https://twitter.com/AnthropicAI/status/2072106151890809341\">US Commerce Dept Lifts Export Controls on Fable 5</a>\n   544→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Twitter</span>\n   545→                    </div>\n   546→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   547→                        Major policy shift as US Department of Commerce lifts export controls on advanced AI models Fable 5 and Mythos 5, potentially enabling broader international access.\n   548→                    </div>\n   549→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   550→                        <a href=\"https://twitter.com/AnthropicAI/status/2072106151890809341\">Anthropic AI</a>\n   551→                        | 2026-07-01\n   552→                    </div>\n   553→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   554→                        <span class=\"tag\">export-controls</span>\n   555→                        <span class=\"tag\">Fable-5</span>\n   556→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI-policy</span>\n   557→                    </div>\n   558→                </div>\n   559→\n   560→                <div class=\"item\">\n   561→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   562→                        <a href=\"https://zcode.z.ai/en\">ZCode: Harness for GLM-5.2</a>\n   563→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">Platform</span>\n   564→                    </div>\n   565→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   566→                        ZCode launches as a development harness for GLM-5.2 model, gaining significant attention on Hacker News (505 points) and reflecting continued ecosystem development around large language models.\n   567→                    </div>\n   568→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   569→                        <a href=\"https://zcode.z.ai/en\">z.ai</a>\n   570→                        | 2026-07-01\n   571→                    </div>\n   572→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   573→                        <span class=\"tag\">GLM-5.2</span>\n   574→                        <span class=\"tag\">development-tools</span>\n   575→                        <span class=\"tag\">LLM-harness</span>\n   576→                    </div>\n   577→                </div>\n   578→\n   579→                <div class=\"item\">\n   580→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   581→                        <a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/gaming-industry/open-source-game-engine-godot-will-no-longer-accept-ai-authored-code-contributions-we-cant-trust-heavy-users-of-ai-to-understand-their-code-enough-to-fix-it/\">Godot Bans AI-Authored Code Contributions</a>\n   582→                        <span class=\"source-badge\">TechMedia</span>\n   583→                    </div>\n   584→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   585→                        Popular game engine Godot announces it will no longer accept AI-authored code contributions, citing concerns about code understanding and maintenance.\n   586→                    </div>\n   587→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   588→                        <a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/gaming-industry/open-source-game-engine-godot-will-no-longer-accept-ai-authored-code-contributions-we-cant-trust-heavy-users-of-ai-to-understand-their-code-enough-to-fix-it/\">PC Gamer</a>\n   589→                        | 2026-07-01\n   590→                    </div>\n   591→                    <div class=\"tags\">\n   592→                        <span class=\"tag\">AI-code</span>\n   593→                        <span class=\"tag\">open-source</span>\n   594→                        <span class=\"tag\">Godot</span>\n   595→                    </div>\n   596→                </div>\n   597→\n   598→                <div class=\"item\">\n   599→                    <div class=\